   Wat je gaat doen As an Orderpicker at GEODIS in Venlo, you are responsible for picking and preparing high-quality electronic products for shipment. You will work in a clean and modern warehouse where every day is different. You can work between 32 and 40 hours per week in fixed day shifts from 07:00 to 16:00 or from 09:00 to 18:00. Part-time work is also possible.

Your daily tasks include:- Picking customer orders using a hand scanner;
- Packing orders and preparing them for shipment;
- Working with an Electric Pallet Truck (EPT);
- Checking products for quality and quantity;
- Moving goods within the warehouse;
- Loading and unloading goods;
- Following safety and quality procedures;
- Working together with your colleagues to reach daily targets.

Do you have a valid forklift or reach truck certificate? Then you can also use these skills in other warehouse departments within GEODIS.

 Wat we je bieden - Salary up to €16.20 gross per hour;
- Guaranteed 32 to 40 hours per week;
- Full-time and part-time opportunities;
- Fixed day shifts;
- Temporary contract with the possibility of a permanent contract;
- 8% holiday allowance;
- 24 vacation days based on a full-time contract;
- Travel allowance of €0.25 per kilometre, up to €12.50 per working day;
- Career growth opportunities within GEODIS;
- A modern, clean, and safe warehouse;
- Good training and a complete onboarding program.
- Through Start People, you will receive the same employment conditions as employees who work directly for GEODIS.

 Functie-eisen You enjoy working in a warehouse and like to stay active. You also:- Are available for at least 32 hours per week;
- Have warehouse or logistics experience (preferred);
- Have EPT experience (preferred);
- Speak Dutch, English, or German;
- Have your own transportation;
- Are physically fit;
- Can provide a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG).

